{"summary":"Rejected the amendment after verifying the cited regression. The specific end-to-end test it names is currently passing; the workspace test suite is red for a different failure, so this amendment misidentifies the problem and does not justify a code change on its own.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-9-1e2c5c9d","decision":"reject","rationale":"The amendment’s core claim is incorrect. Running `cargo test sad_rapid_water_changes_cause_instability --workspace --tests -- --nocapture` passes, and the test reports instability increasing to `0.3857`, well above the asserted `> 0.1` threshold in `crates/tank_core/tests/end_to_end.rs`. Running the full `cargo test --workspace --tests` command does currently fail, but due to a different test (`event_generation_warm_overfed_weak_aeration` in `crates/tank_core/tests/events.rs`), not the water-change instability scenario cited here. Because this amendment is based on a misdiagnosed failure, it should be rejected."}]}